        "Harald Rose",
        "Knut Urban",
        "Maximilian Haider"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Correcting spherical aberration made sub-angstrom electron microscopy practical, transforming structural studies of materials and matter at atomic scales.",
        "attribution": "Rose's optical theory and design, together with Urban and Haider's development and realization of correctors, form a strong theory-to-instrument contribution.",
        "maturity": "The instruments have been used and refined over decades, with broad and sustained impact across microscopy.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The division of credit between the early theoretical work and the engineering and experimental realization would need careful historical assessment."
        ]
      }
    },
